Conflicts: howdy
Description: face authentication for PAM
 Howdy Next authenticates a user by face recognition through PAM. It
 provides the pam_howdy.so module, the howdy command, and a setuid helper
 that prepares root-controlled copies of the configuration and enrolled
 models for the unprivileged authentication process.
 .
 OpenCV 5 is bundled in a private directory, because Debian does not
 package it. The face-recognition models are downloaded and verified by
 "howdy download-models".
 .
 Face authentication is weaker than a password. The PAM profile is installed
 disabled; enable it with "pam-auth-update --enable howdy" after enrolling a
 face with "howdy add".
